    {
      "id": "3yltkiw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOUND"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a longitudinal mechanical wave that requires a material medium to propagate and cannot travel through a vacuum.",
        "The speed of sound is highest in solids, moderate in liquids, and lowest in gases.",
        "Human hearing is sensitive to frequencies between 20 Hz and 20,000 Hz (20 kHz).",
        "An echo requires a minimum distance of 17.2 metres from the reflecting surface at room temperature.",
        "Ultrasonic sound waves (above 20 kHz) are used in SONAR, medical imaging, and industrial cleaning."
      ],
      "id": "eimq1zq"
    },
